  "conclusion": {
    "analysis_sha256": "1522c2aff07ff995313bfbc7f0153d5a71d153a087e820feb669fef85fa15037",
    "finding": "The experiment does not support optimizer reset as the primary explanation. Continuing PPO on the same corpus also lowers this validation score with original optimizer and critic preserved.",
    "interpretation": "Results are compatible with limited generalization during continued optimization and regression from a validation-selected high point. They do not isolate the share due to each, nor establish a population-level performance loss. Sampled validation decline shows the pattern is not limited to greedy argmax flips.",
    "model_promotion": false,
    "observations": [
      "All six +50k endpoints are below the selected parent on both greedy and sampled validation. Retain-Adam greedy 21/23, reset-Adam 24/22, reset-Adam-and-critic 21/23 out of 42; parent 26.",
      "Retained-Adam and Adam-reset arms improve TRAIN greedy and sampled wins in both schedules, while validation wins decline. Critic-reset TRAIN greedy changes are mixed.",
      "Retaining Adam does not consistently improve either validation mode relative to resetting Adam; critic-reset sampled scores are lower in both schedules, but greedy differences have no consistent direction.",
      "Calibrated critic MC error is near the original in schedule a (.1215 versus .1230) and worse in b (.1362 versus .1175), not a uniform calibration failure.",
      "Final policy agreement is89.7\u201393.3 percent on 808 fixed public TRAIN states. Exact original continuation in schedule a loses 7 prior greedy validation wins and gains 2.",
      "Original parent was selected among six historical specialist checkpoints; new endpoints are fixed. Repeated evaluation of the same 42 cases does not create fresh evidence.",
      "All 7,293 evaluationgames and 220,113 actions passed exact headless replay; all 36 checkpoints strictly restored; all 300,000 decisions trained, zero skipped or failed episodes."
    ],
    "policy_drift_sha256": "3369f134d5f9e32ebc2092cadec15d1e668f4cd8bfb4c7afaee4cafc6d4b252b",
    "recommendation": "Retain the 250k parent. Prioritize more independent Vantom training fights and a frozen development panel; measure new representation/reward treatments from a common earlier initializer at fixed budgets/checkpoints. A conservative continuation learning-rate comparison is a separate targeted follow-up if preserving this exact actor is the objective. Do not attribute earlier feature/shaping results solely to reset handling.",
    "status": "complete",
    "uncertainty": "Two continuation schedules of one preselected parent, not independent pretrained models; same 101 TRAIN and 42 reused validation campaigns. All six greedy endpoint-versus-parent bootstrap intervals include or touch zero. No correction for all repeated comparisons. Reserved 57 test openings remain unopened.",
    "verification_sha256": "c7850a29bd5ec2fa122650153fdb3c3ea57e7929a5f480b57570fb8729b20c9b"
  },
